    description: "## Statement (also in `fields.statement`)\n\nWhen a documented contract — spec text in `docs/hypergumbo-spec.md`, JSON schema in `docs/schema.json`, dataclass declaration in `ir.py` / `datamodels.py`, or pass-catalog entry — declares a behavior, shape, or field, the implementation must either conform OR the contract must be updated. Drift between any two of (spec doc, schema.json, dataclass declarations, producer code, consumer code, CI gates) is a violated form. Vigilance is not sufficient; the discipline requires mechanical enforcement at PR time.\n\n## Root cause (also in `fields.root_cause`)\n\nNo CI or pre-commit gate currently asserts:\n\n- (a) hypergumbo's own behavior map validates against `docs/schema.json`;\n- (b) every spec-declared field has a non-trivial producer OR a documented null-condition;\n- (c) schema migrations include a conformance audit of all linkers/analyzers/consumers;\n- (d) catalog vs runtime pass-id naming agrees.\n\nEach drift bug is filed as its own item because no member of the discipline existed to catch it pre-merge. The recurrences indicate this is an architectural axis, not a sequence of independent oversights.\n\n## Members\n\n- `INV-piroh` (P2 violated) — Hypergumbo's own behavior map fails schema validation. Two distinct gaps: `js_module.py:811` hardcodes `line=0` (violates `Edge.line minimum: 1`); 3 top-level keys (`entrypoints`, `sketch_precomputed`, `usage_contexts`) produced but not in `BehaviorMap.properties`. **No CI gate currently validates hypergumbo output against its own schema.** This is the canonical example of (a).\n- `INV-bovif` (P2 violated) — 4 framework linkers (event-sourcing, http, graphql-resolver, database-query) emit symbols but ZERO edges. Schema 0.2.2 → 0.8.0 migration moved framework-specific node kinds onto `meta.framework_role`, but only `message_queue.py` and `websocket.py` migrated their edge-construction code; the other 4 still target deleted kind names and silently emit nothing. Example of (c) — no migration-conformance audit existed.\n- `WI-bujim` (P3 todo_soft) — `features[]` is documented in the spec at `docs/hypergumbo-spec.md:798-802` as \"named slices\" with a full sub-shape, but `schema.py:101` hardcodes `[]` with no producer. Example of (b) — spec-declared field with no producer.\n- `INV-tofur` (P3 violated) — `AnalysisRun.repo_fingerprint` algorithm is fully specified at `docs/hypergumbo-spec.md:378-384` (sha256 of git_head + sorted dirty-file content hashes), but no producer implements it; 100% null on 133 runs. Adjacent `_get_repo_state_hash()` in `sketch_embeddings.py:1278-1376` uses a different algorithm for cache sharding (root cause of INV-magul). Example of (b).\n- `INV-morag` (P2 violated) — Pass-ID naming asymmetry between the hypergumbo catalog (`-ts-v1` suffix) and runtime `AnalysisRun.pass` values (`-v1` suffix). 40 catalog names absent in runs; 99 run names absent in catalog. Example of (d) — no name-agreement check.\n- `WI-busij` (P4 todo_soft) — **The closest existing partial fix.** Articulates one fragment of the discipline: pre-commit detection of new multi-value field additions to core dataclasses (`Edge`, `Symbol`, `Span`, anything in `ir.py` or `datamodels.py`). Its scope is narrow (field-add only), but its shape is exactly what this META asks for at the broader level. The implementation work for WI-busij becomes one piece of this META's closure.\n\n## Why this is an invariant, not six independent fixes\n\nEach member is a different manifestation of the same architectural gap: the spec/schema/code triangle has no mechanical reconciliation. Fixing INV-piroh's specific `line=0` bug doesn't prevent the next producer from emitting an unschematized field. Implementing INV-tofur's `repo_fingerprint` producer doesn't catch the next spec-declared-but-unimplemented field. Fixing INV-bovif's 4 linkers doesn't prevent the next schema migration from leaving consumers behind.\n\nThe shared discipline is **\"every spec/schema declaration has a verifiable producer + consumer at CI time, and migrations include a conformance audit\"**. WI-busij is the partial form of one branch of that.\n\n## Closure criterion\n\nThe META closes `satisfied` when:\n\n1. A CI gate validates hypergumbo's own behavior map against `docs/schema.json` (closes (a), validates INV-piroh stays closed).\n2. A `check-spec-implementation-drift` script (analog of `check-edge-type-drift`) asserts every spec-declared field has a producer or documented null-condition (closes (b), catches future WI-bujim / INV-tofur cases).\n3. Schema-migration playbook exists requiring conformance audit across linkers/analyzers (closes (c)).\n4. Pass-catalog vs `AnalysisRun.pass` agreement check at CI (closes (d)).\n5. WI-busij implementation lands as part of (1) or as its own narrow gate.\n\nEach member item closes via its own fix; the META closes when the mechanical-check discipline is in place to prevent recurrence.\n\n## Related but separate\n\n- **Identity META** (`INV-dajaf`): identity-field honesty is a separate axis. `WI-fanun` is under the identity META, not here, because the field's correctness is about identity semantics; if it were just \"this declared field is empty\", it would be a member here.\n- **`ADR-0023` / `check-edge-type-drift`**: existing precedent for mechanical drift checking. The CI gate proposed here is the same shape, applied at the spec/schema/dataclass boundary instead of the edge-type registry.\n- **`ADR-0024` (axis declaration template)**: orthogonal — about new multi-value fields specifically. This META covers all declared fields and shapes."  # 9058
